The attached image illustrates the enhanced antibody response induced by Nano-11 as a vaccine adjuvant. Box plots compare anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone, rPA with aluminum hydroxide (AH) at 200, 50, and 12.5 µg/dose, and rPA with Nano-11 at 200, 50, and 12.5 µg/dose. The data show that all Nano-11 and AH formulations significantly increased antibody titers compared to rPA alone, with Nano-11 inducing similar or even higher titers than AH, particularly at lower doses. This demonstrates Nano-11's potent adjuvant effect on antigen-specific antibody production.